      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name}\n\nI tested this avatar and this world with my friend who indeed has an AMD ryzen 9800x and I can assure you it's not the world nor the avatar. So an excuse of it's just BIRP being single threaded is not a good explanation when his system is running better with lower specs than me. I have superior multi-threaded and single core performance. It seems like BIRP doesn't know how to properly utilize CPUs with hybrid architectures and would rather choke the core out. Perhaps it doesn't know how to utilize the cache effectively with the hybrid architectures and it's continuously throwing errors so the core has to reprocess it again. Who knows. All I know that it's an issue with CPUs that have hybrid architectures. Never has happened once to my with CPUs that don't.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-10-28T14:46:59.789Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The game chokes out one P-core no matter what I do. CPU affinity doesn't matter as well as turning off Hyper-Threading. I get superior performance at extreme settings in every other game I play. There Should be no reason I get 165+fps in Destiny 2 (Ancient Game Engine) but this game has issues lol.\n\nSpecs:\n\nCPU:14900KF\n\nRAM: DDR5 CL26 26-36-36-66\n\nGPU's: RTX 4080 (Primary \"For Game Rendering\")\n\nRTX 3060ti (Secondary \"For Monitor Outputs + Misc. Application Offload\")\n\nSSD: Samsung 990 PRO\n\nMotherBoard: MSI MPG Z790I Edge WiFi (MS-7E03)\n\nMy findings have concluded that even non x3d chips like the 9800X do not have this issue and multithread appropriately. I have found that my old Intel 10700k does not have an issue with threaded load distribution too. This issue has occurred to my knowledge since builds that were released as far as 2023. May this performance issue please be looked at for individuals with a hybrid architecture? (12th, 13th, 14th Gen + Core Ultra 3, 5, 7, 9 Gen)\n\nThanks!",
